{"verdict":{"vulnerable":true,"confidence":0.65,"cwe":["CWE-20"],"severity":"medium","summary":"Attacker-controlled int size (line 1) reaches sink ret->size = size (line 6) without validation of the input value itself; guard line 3 checks derived unsigned alloc_size, not size, and does not apply to derived pointer ret at sink (mismatch: guard object alloc_size line 3 vs sink object ret line 6 with source size)."},"evidence":[{"file":null,"function":"TfLiteIntArrayCreate","location":{"start_line":1,"end_line":6},"snippet":"TfLiteIntArray* TfLiteIntArrayCreate(int size) {
  size_t alloc_size = TfLiteIntArrayGetSizeInBytes(size);
  ...
  ret->size = size;","reason":"Source int size at line 1; derived ret assigned line 4 via alloc_size line 2; sink ret->size=size at line 6 writes unvalidated attacker-controlled input through derived pointer ret."},{"file":null,"function":"TfLiteIntArrayCreate","location":{"start_line":3,"end_line":6},"snippet":"  if (alloc_size <= 0) return NULL;
  ...
  ret->size = size;","reason":"Explicit mismatch: guard checks alloc_size (line 3) but sink dereferences derived pointer ret (line 6) with source size; no quoted validation of size relative to ret->size at sink, and derived-pointer validity never paired with size check."}],"notes":{"assumptions":["TfLiteIntArrayGetSizeInBytes definition not shown"],"limitations":["Inferred across >3 lines from parameter to sink","TfLiteIntArrayGetSizeInBytes unquoted so arithmetic/overflow unverified","Derived ret validity at sink not quoted together with size validation"]}}

